<tmc-service-inc>
<pub id="RM0550J">
<servcat id="10">
<name>Body &amp; Electrical</name>
<section id="1002S_S000E" variety="S000E">
<name>Vehicle Surroundings Monitor</name>
<ttl id="1002S_S000E_742B9_T003J" variety="T003J">
<name>Intelligent Parking Assist System</name>
<para id="RM0000021NY006X" category="C" type-id="80395" name-id="672E6-00" from="200612" to="200912">
<dtccode>C1627</dtccode>
<dtcname>Height Sensor Voltage Malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000021NY006X_09" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00007ND00000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The height control sensor assembly (rear) is connected to the television camera controller. The height control sensor assembly (rear) is also shared with the lighting system (automatic leveling). In this case, power is supplied to the height control sensor assembly (rear) by the headlight leveling computer assembly. This DTC is output when the television camera controller self-diagnosis judges that the power supply voltage to the height control sensor assembly (rear) is abnormal.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" align="left">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="3.08in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Diagnosis Description</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C1627</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Height Sensor Power Source Voltage Drop</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Height Sensor Power Source Voltage Rise</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Headlight Leveling Computer Assembly</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Wire harness between headlight leveling computer assembly and television camera controller</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Television Camera Controller</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Wire harness and connector between television camera controller and height control sensor assembly (rear)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000021NY006X_10" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00007NE00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E144417J01" width="7.106578999in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000021NY006X_11" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___00007NF00000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When the battery terminal is disconnected, perform the setting operations required when the battery terminal is removed and installed. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000001LYW00PX"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Depending on the parts replaced or the work performed during inspection, registration settings for other systems may be necessary in addition to the intelligent parking assist system. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM00000304S000X"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the headlight leveling computer assembly is replaced, perform registration setting of the lighting system. (see <xref label="Seep03" href="RM0000030GL000X"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If registration/setting becomes necessary while proceeding with the inspection, perform the registration/setting work before proceeding to the next inspection step.  </ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000021NY006X_12" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM0000021NY006X_12_0027" proc-id="RM0550J___00007NG00000">
<testtitle>Recheck DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check DTC</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), read the DTCs by following the screen display. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000OCQ007X"/>)</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Select "Clear" on the screen to clear the data. </ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Turn IG OFF.</ptxt>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Recheck DTC</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Start the engine, check the DTCs again, and proceed to the following destination.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt/>
</specitem>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.01in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.12in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>"C1627" is output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>No DTC Output (Normal)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000021NY006X_12_0029" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM0000021NY006X_12_0034" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000021NY006X_12_0029" proc-id="RM0550J___00007NI00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Headlight Leveling Computer Assembly - Television Camera Controller)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Pre-inspection Preparation</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Disconnect the headlight leveling computer assembly connector.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E141970J01" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Disconnect connector A of the television camera controller shown in the illustration.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E141824J11" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Resistance Inspection</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance of the wire harness between the headlight leveling computer assembly and television camera controller.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.65in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.45in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.03in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A24 (HB+) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>10 kΩ or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A23 (HGND) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>10 kΩ or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>12(SBR) - A24(HB+)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>21(SGR) - A23(HGND)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000021NY006X_12_0030" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000021NY006X_12_0035" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000021NY006X_12_0030" proc-id="RM0550J___00007NJ00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Headlight Leveling Computer Assembly (HB+, HGND)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Voltage Inspection</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E141824J03" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<test2>
<ptxt>Connect the headlight leveling computer assembly connector and, using SST (Toyota electrical tester), with connector A of the vehicle side wire harness shown in the illustration disconnected, measure the voltage between each terminal from the back side of the connector.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.65in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.45in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.03in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A24(HB+) - A23(HGND)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>4.75 to 5.25 V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000021NY006X_12_0031" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000021NY006X_12_0036" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
